  "designDecisions": [
    "Use the supplied dark/light seed palette, namespaced to avoid collisions with historical Pixel Deck work.",
    "Use Inter in editable Figma text because Segoe UI and Segoe UI Variable are unavailable to the connected Figma environment; specify Segoe UI Variable with Segoe UI fallback for WPF implementation.",
    "Use Cascadia Mono for timer and numeric data; it is available in the target Figma environment.",
    "Build local components instead of importing Material 3 or Simple Design System because their geometry, token model, platform conventions, and remote ownership do not match the Windows/WPF deliverable.",
    "Treat selected-active state and running state as independent visual attributes.",
    "Treat combined overlay as presentation only and preserve each timer's run state, visibility, and separate position.",
    "Model standalone Project Records as an implementation-ready information-architecture change; current production embeds records in the dashboard expander.",
    "Show shortcut conflicts as both an inline proposed state and a save-time confirmation note because current production validates after Save.",
    "Keep frequent timer actions above the fold; move global appearance/configuration into a right inspector with progressive disclosure.",
    "Do not reuse Pixel Deck styling or assets; historical screenshots are before-state evidence only.",
    "Give Delete confirmation safe initial focus on Cancel even though current production does not explicitly set it.",
    "Recommend disabling Clock Reset because the current controller leaves it visible but no-ops the command.",
    "Interpret compact overlay as intrinsic short-format composition rather than a new persisted compact-mode setting.",
    "Use live editable Figma clones for the After comparisons and explicit local source labels for Before while the external Figma image-upload blocker remains; do not invent substitute screenshots."
  ]
